<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Njeri wants the greatest volume of an open box made from a square sheet <m>{24}</m> cm by <m>{24}</m> cm by cutting squares of side <m>x</m> cm from the corners. Her working has one mistake.</p><ol><li>The height of the box is <m>x</m> cm, and <m>x</m> must be between <m>0</m> and <m>{12}</m>.</li><li>Each side of the base is <m>({24} - x)</m> cm, so <m>V = x({24} - x)^2</m>.</li><li><m>V = {x^3-48 x^2+576 x}</m></li><li><m>\dfrac{dV}{dx} = {3 x^2-96 x+576}</m></li><li><m>\dfrac{dV}{dx} = (3x - {24})(x - {24}) = 0</m>, so <m>x = {8}</m> or <m>x = {24}</m>.</li><li><m>\dfrac{d^2V}{dx^2} = {6 x-96}</m>. At <m>x = {8}</m> this is <m>{-48}</m>, which is negative, so <m>x = {8}</m> gives the greatest volume.</li><li><m>V = {8} \times ({24} - {8})^2 = 2048</m> cm<m>^3</m></li></ol><p>(a) Which step has the mistake?</p><div>[ Step 1 | Step 2 | Step 3 | Step 4 | Step 5 | Step 6 | Step 7 ]  </div><p>(b) Give the correct greatest volume.</p><div><fillin characters="6" name="ans2"/> cm<m>^3</m>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) The mistake is in Step 2. Cutting a square from each corner shortens each edge of the base at both ends, so the base is <m>({24} - 2x)</m> cm square, not <m>({24} - x)</m> cm. Every later step follows from the wrong model.</p><p>(b) The correct working is:</p><ol><li>The height of the box is <m>x</m> cm, and <m>x</m> must be between <m>0</m> and <m>{12}</m>.</li><li>Each side of the base is <m>({24} - 2x)</m> cm, so <m>V = x({24} - 2x)^2</m>.</li><li><m>V = {4 x^3-96 x^2+576 x}</m></li><li><m>\dfrac{dV}{dx} = {12 x^2-192 x+576}</m></li><li><m>\dfrac{dV}{dx} = (6x - {24})(2x - {24}) = 0</m>, so <m>x = {4}</m> or <m>x = {12}</m>.</li><li><m>\dfrac{d^2V}{dx^2} = {24 x-192}</m>. At <m>x = {4}</m> this is <m>{-96}</m>, which is negative, so <m>x = {4}</m> gives the greatest volume.</li><li><m>V = {4} \times ({24} - {8})^2 = 1024</m> cm<m>^3</m></li></ol></p></solution>
    <answer><p>Step 2</p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>1024</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>